 source('CA_GOV_66315','California Government Code §66315 occupancy and rental limits','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&sectionNum=66315.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2024-03-25','§66315','Section 66314 supplies the maximum standards for a single-family-lot ADU; an owner-occupant requirement may not be imposed except for the qualified-buyer sale path, while rentals may be restricted to terms longer than 30 days.'),
 source('CA_GOV_66317','California Government Code §66317 ministerial process','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&sectionNum=66317.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2025-01-01','§66317','A permitting agency considers and approves or denies a complete ADU application ministerially within 60 days and supplies a complete defect list and remedies upon denial.'),
 source('CA_GOV_66321','California Government Code §66321 size and height floors','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&sectionNum=66321.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2025-01-01','§66321(b)','Local size, coverage, FAR, open-space, minimum-lot-size, and front-setback rules cannot preclude an 800-square-foot ADU with four-foot side and rear setbacks. Local maxima must permit 850 square feet, or 1,000 with more than one bedroom. Detached height floors are 16 feet, 18 feet under transit or multistory-multifamily predicates, plus up to two roof-pitch feet under the transit predicate; attached height is 25 feet or the primary-dwelling zoning limit, whichever is lower.'),
 source('CA_GOV_66322','California Government Code §66322 parking and nonconformity','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&sectionNum=66322.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2025-01-01','§66322','Parking is prohibited for enumerated transit, historic, conversion, permit, car-share, and paired-primary-application cases. Unaffected nonconforming zoning conditions and non-safety building conditions cannot be required to be corrected as an ADU condition.'),
 source('CA_GOV_66323_2026','California Government Code §66323 operative 2026 state-mandated units','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&sectionNum=66323.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2026-01-01','§66323','In 2026, the state-mandated single-family combination includes one conversion ADU, one JADU, and one detached new-construction ADU up to 800 square feet. Multifamily conversion units are at least one and up to 25 percent of existing units; detached units are up to eight for existing multifamily, capped by existing units, or up to two for proposed multifamily. Only standards authorized by §66323 apply.'),
 source('CA_GOV_66333','California Government Code §§66333-66339 JADUs','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displayText.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&division=1.&title=7.&part=&chapter=13.&article=3.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2026-01-01','§§66333-66339','A JADU is no more than 500 square feet within a proposed or existing single-family residence, has an efficiency kitchen and exterior access, may share sanitation, requires owner occupancy only when sanitation is shared subject to entity exceptions, requires rentals longer than 30 days, and requires no parking.'),
 source('CA_GOV_66341','California Government Code §66341 qualified nonprofit conveyance','https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=GOV&sectionNum=66341.','OPERATIVE_STATUTE','2024-03-25','§66341','Separate sale is generally outside the ordinary path; §66341 supplies a bounded qualified-nonprofit and qualified-buyer conveyance path with deed and occupancy conditions.'),
